# Melee's two effects last "this combat" (CR 506.1, 511.3): Combat Celebrant, exerted as it attacks, gives the turn an
# additional combat phase (CR 500.8). In the first, Bot1 casts Melee and chooses Bot2's blocks: Crimson Kobolds blocks the
# Celebrant. In the second, Bot2 declares its own blocks again - Phyrexian Walker blocks one Memnite - and the other Memnite,
# unblocked, is not untapped and removed from combat: it deals Bot2 1 damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Combat Celebrant
Memnite
Memnite
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Black Lotus
Mountain
Melee
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Phyrexian Walker
Crimson Kobolds
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Combat Celebrant.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Phyrexian Walker.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Crimson Kobolds.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Combat Celebrant > Bot2)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Melee.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Block(Crimson Kobolds > Combat Celebrant)
[T3 Bot1.EndCombat]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Step = BeginCombat
Bot1.Attack(Memnite#1 > Bot2; Memnite#2 > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Phyrexian Walker > Memnite)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Graveyard = Crimson Kobolds
